Cell["\<\
A linear system perturbed by a Gaussian stochastic input (does not need to be \
white) will produce a Gaussian stochastic output. If the output from a system \
driven by a Gaussian stochastic input is non Gaussian (as here) then this is \
clear evidence that the system is nonlinear.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7839498484627447`*^9, 
  3.783949972186845*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6a6b6485-ef77-4dc4-b125-\
a8219cc36f9a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Compare input and output probability distribution functions ", \
"Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.784051136768323*^9, 3.784051161105425*^9}, {
  3.784051196536063*^9, 
  3.784051199382352*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d3da95b9-4fa8-4331-ade2-\
cd4f5d4fc6af"],

Cell["\<\
Lets calculate the smoothed input and output probability distribution \
functions:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.783949157686884*^9, 3.7839492097692595`*^9}, 
   3.783949271551796*^9, 3.7839496546798625`*^9, {3.783949799430415*^9, 
